# lauren-di — everything that must never be committed.
#
# Every path below is one of three things: a build product that is reproducible
# from a clean checkout (`dist/`, `site/`), a cache the next `nox` session
# recreates (`.nox/`, `.pytest_cache/`, `__pycache__/`), or a tool's local
# scratch. `nox -s clean` deletes the same set from a working tree, and
# `tests/unit/test_gitignore_contract.py` checks this file in both directions:
# every artefact nox creates must be ignored here, and no tracked deliverable
# may be.
#
# Deliberately *not* ignored, although they are generated: `docs/reference.md`
# and `llms-full.txt`. They are reviewed in the diff and verified by CI
# (`nox -s docs_contract llms_check`), so they are tracked like source — see
# AGENTS.md ground rule 4.
#
# Also deliberately not ignored: `prds/`. It is the specification this library
# is written against (CONTRIBUTING.md §Layout), not planning scratch.

# --- Byte-compiled code ----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*$py.class

# --- Build products --------------------------------------------------------
# `nox -s build` and `python -m build` write both; setuptools leaves the rest.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/
MANIFEST

# --- Documentation site ----------------------------------------------------
# `nox -s docs` renders `docs/` + `mkdocs.yml` into `site/`.
site/

# --- Test, coverage and type-checker caches --------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- Nox virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------
# One virtualenv per session, recreated on demand.
.nox/

# --- Virtualenvs and local environment -------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Editors and OS noise --------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Agent and tool scratch ------------------------------------------------
.agenthicc/
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/
.codemap
# A recorded agent session: `cassette.jsonl` is a verbatim transcript and
# `approvals.jsonl` its tool-approval log. Neither is a test fixture — nothing
# in the repository reads the directory (grep finds no consumer), and it dirties
# the working tree on every run. Deliberately *not* the same decision as
# `prds/evidence/`, which is tracked because PRDs 02-08 cite its probe ids.
tests/.cassette/
